("H","## Systematic survey of reference genome usage in publicly available FVB RNA-seq studies"),
(KEEP,"We searched NCBI GEO to examine how FVB RNA-seq studies have been processed [CITE Barrett 2013]. The search was performed in June 2026. We used the terms \"FVB\", \"expression profiling by high throughput sequencing\", and \"Mus musculus\". This search returned 1,047 GEO series."),
(KEEP,"We included studies that generated RNA-seq data from FVB mice. We considered FVB/NJ, FVB/N, and studies that reported the strain only as \"FVB\". We excluded series in which FVB was not the main experimental strain. We also excluded studies in which FVB appeared only as a transgenic host background or as a cell-line origin. Studies with fewer than three samples were also excluded. Series without accessible data-processing metadata were excluded."),
(KEEP,"After manual review, «survey_total|d» GEO series met the inclusion criteria. These series formed the survey cohort. For each series, we retrieved the !Sample_data_processing and !Series_data_processing fields from GEO SOFT metadata."),
(KEEP,"Each study was assigned to one of three categories. This included explicit mention of GRCm38, GRCm39, mm10, mm39, C57BL/6, or standard aligner paths containing these assemblies. This category also included legacy mm9 annotations when they were reported in GEO metadata, because mm9 is likewise a standard C57BL/6-derived mouse reference assembly. The third category was not reported. This was used when data-processing text was available but no reference-genome keyword was identified."),
(KEEP,"Classification was performed in priority order. Strain-aware classification took priority over stated B6. Stated B6 took priority over not reported. This prevented strain-aware studies from being misclassified if they also mentioned a standard assembly. Because this survey relied on public GEO metadata, absence of a keyword was interpreted as absence of reporting rather than definitive proof that a correction strategy was not used."),
("H","<!-- BEGIN generated/methods_datasets.md (rendered from revision_v2/manifest/manifest.tsv by revision_v2/scripts/render_methods_datasets.py; do not edit by hand) -->"),
