("CORR","A gene was included in the bias catalog if it met two criteria. First, its bias had to be at least 0.5 log₂ units in at least two of the four non-tumour tissues. These tissues were adipose tissue, hypothalamus, liver, and skin. Second, the gene had to be present in the FVB GTF."),
(KEEP,"The FVB GTF filter was used to restrict the catalog to genes with a well-defined FVB locus. Genes absent from the FVB GTF usually came from regions where g2gtools coordinate conversion failed. These were often Y-chromosome or pseudogene loci with unusual annotation boundaries. Many also had zero FVB/NJ SNP density. Apparent bias in these genes was not interpreted as SNP-mediated read-mapping bias."),
