meth+=[
("H","## Predictor analysis"),
(KEEP,"We evaluated four candidate predictors of SNP-mediated reference-genome mapping bias. These were FVB/NJ SNP density, gene length, gene biotype, and mean expression level."),
(KEEP,"SNP density was calculated from the FVB/NJ SNP VCF. SNPs were counted within the Ensembl gene body, from start to end coordinates inclusive. SNP count was divided by gene length in kilobases. Indels were not included because the personalised reference encoded SNP substitutions only."),
(KEEP,"Gene length was calculated in base pairs. It was log₁₀-transformed for analysis. Gene biotype was taken from the Ensembl 110 annotation. Biotypes were grouped as protein-coding, lncRNA, pseudogene, miRNA, or other. Mean expression was calculated as mean log₂ CPM across samples in the naive arm."),
("CORR","Gene-level predictors were compared with mean per-gene bias across the tissues in which the gene was tested. Associations were tested with Spearman rank correlation. The correlation restricted to genes tested in all four tissues is also reported."),
("H","## F1 allele-specific expression analysis"),
(KEEP,"F1 hybrid datasets were used to test allele-level reference bias. The datasets were GSE200632 and GSE293440. Reads were aligned to the GRCm39 B6 reference under naive and WASP-filtered conditions."),
("NEW-F1","Allele-specific read counts were obtained with GATK ASEReadCounter v4.6.2.0 [CITE McKenna 2010]. Counts were extracted at the «f1_site_set_n|,d» exonic sites at which FVB/NJ is homozygous for the alternative allele in the Mouse Genomes Project REL-2021 calls — the site set of the sample-identity check — at every one of which an F1 animal is expected to be heterozygous. Because ASEReadCounter evaluates only sites whose genotype in the supplied VCF is heterozygous, the genotype field of this site set was rewritten to 0/1 for this analysis (repository file `fvbnj_homalt_exonic.hetGT.vcf.gz`). The minimum mapping quality and base quality were 20."),
(KEEP,"Sites were retained if they met two filters. Total read depth had to be at least 20. Both reference and alternate alleles had to have at least three supporting reads."),
(KEEP,"The FVB allele fraction was calculated for each site as:"),
(KEEP,"alt_count / total_count"),
(KEEP,"In B6-reference coordinates, the alternate allele corresponds to the FVB/NJ allele at these sites. For each sample, the mean FVB allele fraction was calculated across all passing sites. The expected value under unbiased mapping is 0.50."),
("CORR","Deviation from 0.50 was tested with a one-sample t-test. Group-level means and standard errors were calculated separately for naive and WASP-filtered alignments."),
("NEW-F1","To attribute the WASP effect to one allele, the reads removed by the WASP filter at each retained site were counted separately for the reference and the alternative allele (repository file `f1_wasp_allele_removal.tsv`), and the per-animal mean FVB allele fraction was also computed separately for the retained sites inside the catalog genes and for the other retained sites (paired t-test across animals)."),
("H","## Multi-mapping sensitivity analysis"),
(KEEP,"The primary analysis used the standard featureCounts setting [CITE Liao 2014]. Under this setting, multi-mapping reads are excluded from gene-level counts. These reads are assigned to Unassigned_MultiMapping."),
(KEEP,"We performed a sensitivity analysis to test whether catalog-gene bias depended on multi-mapper exclusion. This analysis used featureCounts with -M --fraction (Subread v2.0.3). In this mode, a read with N equally good alignments contributes a fractional count of 1/N to each mapped locus."),
("PHASE-K1","This analysis was designed to distinguish two mechanisms. The first mechanism was direct SNP misalignment. In this case, FVB reads fail to align, are assigned to an incorrect locus, or remain multi-mappers on both references. Including multi-mapping reads should not strongly reduce the bias."),
(KEEP,"The second mechanism was SNP-induced multi-mapping. In this case, FVB/NJ SNPs reduce the alignment score gap between the correct locus and paralogous loci in the B6 reference. Reads then become multi-mappers and are excluded from unique-only counts. Including multi-mapping reads should partially restore FVB signal in the naive arm."),
("CORR","For each dataset, multi-mapping-inclusive count matrices were generated for the naive arm and the FVB arm. The same BAM files were used as in the primary analysis. The paired-end flag -p was used for GSE123875, GSE123893, and GSE123894. Single-end mode was used for GSE86315 and GSE175625. All other settings matched the primary featureCounts analysis. The B6 GTF was used for all arms."),
(KEEP,"Bias under multi-mapping inclusion was calculated from the resulting count matrices. We used the same edgeR workflow as in the primary analysis [CITE Robinson 2010]."),
(KEEP,"For each gene, we calculated:"),
(KEEP,"Δ = bias_multi − bias_unique"),
(KEEP,"A negative Δ indicates that multi-mapping inclusion restores part of the FVB signal in the naive arm. This pattern is consistent with SNP-induced multi-mapping. A Δ near zero indicates that the bias is largely unchanged. This pattern is consistent with direct SNP misalignment."),
(KEEP,"We also calculated the residual fraction:"),
(KEEP,"residual fraction = bias_multi / bias_unique"),
(KEEP,"This value measures how much of the unique-only bias remains after multi-mapping reads are included."),
("CORR/PHASE-K1","Catalog genes were classified into two mechanistic groups on the mean over tested tissues. Genes with |Δ| > 0.3 log₂ were classified as SNP-induced multi-mapping. Genes with |Δ| ≤ 0.3 log₂ were classified as direct SNP misalignment. The class names describe the usual way in which a bias does or does not respond to fractional counting; the classes are defined operationally by |Δ|, and the |Δ| ≤ 0.3 class also contains loci at which the FVB/NJ reads remain multi-mappers on both references, so that fractional counting shifts the strain ratio on both references alike (*Rps2* in skin; Supplementary Note 2). This |Δ| threshold was used as a pragmatic effect-size cutoff to distinguish genes for which multi-mapping inclusion materially changed the estimated bias from genes whose bias largely persisted after multi-mapper rescue."),
(KEEP,"Full per-gene results are provided in Supplementary Table S2 and Supplementary Note 2. The main manuscript reports the unique-only bias values. These values reflect the bias experienced by investigators using default featureCounts settings."),
("H","## Choice of worked examples and within-strain comparison"),
]
for p in v2sec("methods.md","Choice of worked examples and within-strain comparison"): meth.append(("NEW-WS",p))
