cap+=[("H","**Supplementary Table S2. Catalog of «catalog_n|d» genes consistently showing SNP-mediated reference-genome mapping bias in FVB/B6 comparisons across non-tumour tissue datasets.**"),
("CORR","Full catalog of genes meeting the primary bias criterion. A gene was included if it showed bias ≥ 0.5 log₂ units in at least two of the four non-tumour tissue datasets, namely mesenteric adipose tissue, hypothalamus, liver, and back skin, and was present in the FVB/NJ GTF after g2gtools coordinate conversion. Bias was defined as log₂FC_FVB ref − log₂FC_naive. Genes are sorted by mean_bias descending. The final columns report the multi-mapping sensitivity analysis described in Supplementary Note 2 and the decomposition of the bias. "+v2cap("S2.")[0].split("**Columns:** ",1)[1]+" The |Δ| = 0.3 log₂ cutoff for mechanism class should be interpreted as an effect-size threshold for practical mechanistic annotation rather than as a formal biological boundary."),
("H","**Supplementary Table S3. Sensitivity of the bias catalog to threshold, minimum-tissue count, design and bias definition, and the negative control.**"),
("CORR","Catalog gene counts under a grid of bias thresholds and minimum qualifying-tissue cutoffs, and the negative-control statistics. Bias thresholds were 0.25, 0.5, and 1.0 log₂ units. Minimum qualifying-tissue cutoffs ranged from one to four tissues. The primary catalog criterion used in the main analysis was bias ≥ 0.5 log₂ units in at least two of the four tissues, which yielded «catalog_n|d» genes. These sensitivity results show that the primary «catalog_n|d»-gene catalog is not driven by a single arbitrary parameter choice, although the exact catalog size changes as expected when the threshold or required tissue count is varied.")]
